<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1945</h1><p class="ref-lede">1945 in world history: 72 events, 14 births, 36 deaths, 2 works, 14 states founded and 32 that came to an end. 724 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1941">1941</a><a href="/years/1942">1942</a><a href="/years/1943">1943</a><a href="/years/1944">1944</a><a href="/years/1945" aria-current="page">1945</a><a href="/years/1946">1946</a><a href="/years/1947">1947</a><a href="/years/1948">1948</a><a href="/years/1949">1949</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-12">12 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Red Army launches the Vistula-Oder Offensive</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet forces burst out of their bridgeheads in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and advanced some 500 km in under three weeks. By early February they stood on the Oder, about 70 km from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-16">16 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Hitler moves into the Führerbunker in Berlin</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Adolf Hitler</a> took up residence in the air-raid shelter beneath the Reich Chancellery garden. He directed the final months of the war from there and killed himself in the bunker on 30 April.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/warsaw.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-17">17 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Soviet and Polish troops enter the ruins of Warsaw</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> and the Polish First Army took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a>, abandoned by the Germans. After the crushing of the 1944 Uprising, the Germans had systematically razed the city, destroying about 85 per cent of it.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-world-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-25">25 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Battle of the Bulge ends in Allied victory</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Allied forces restored their line in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardennes">Ardennes</a>, ending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s last major offensive in the west. Fought in bitter winter conditions, it was the costliest American battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-27">27 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Soviet troops liberate Auschwitz</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> soldiers reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswiecim">Auschwitz</a> and found about 7,000 prisoners left behind. Around 1.1 million people, most of them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>, were murdered there. The date is now International <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holocaust">Holocaust</a> Remembrance Day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-30">30 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Soviet submarine sinks the Wilhelm Gustloff</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Torpedoes from submarine S-13 sank the overcrowded German liner in the Baltic as it evacuated refugees and military personnel. An estimated 9,000 died, the greatest loss of life in a single sinking.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-31">31 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Private Eddie Slovik executed for desertion</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Slovik was shot by firing squad in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, the only American soldier executed for desertion since the Civil War. Of many soldiers sentenced to death for the offence, he alone was put to death.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/manila" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manila.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-3">3 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Battle of Manila begins</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">American and Filipino forces entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> to retake it from the Japanese. The month-long battle destroyed much of the city, and around 100,000 Filipino civilians died, many in Japanese massacres.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-4">4 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Yalta Conference opens in Crimea</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Churchill, Roosevelt and Stalin met at the Livadia Palace to plan the end of the war. They agreed on the occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, elections in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, Soviet entry into the Pacific war and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-13">13 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Allied bombers begin the destruction of Dresden</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">British and then American raids over two days created a firestorm that killed about 25,000 people and destroyed the historic centre. The attack's justification has been debated ever since.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/manila" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manila.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-16">16 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">American paratroopers and infantry assault Corregidor</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">US forces landed by parachute and sea on the island fortress at the mouth of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> Bay, lost in 1942. After two weeks of fighting most of its Japanese defenders were dead.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-19">19 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">US Marines land on Iwo Jima</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The 36-day battle killed nearly 7,000 Americans and almost all of the 21,000 Japanese defenders. Joe Rosenthal's photograph of the flag raising on Mount Suribachi became an icon.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-23">23 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">US Marines raise the flag on Mount Suribachi</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Marines planted the US flag on the summit of Iwo Jima's volcano. Joe Rosenthal's photograph of the second, larger flag won the Pulitzer Prize, though the fighting went on for another month.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/rhine" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rhine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-7">7 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">US troops seize the Remagen bridge over the Rhine</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">American soldiers captured the Ludendorff railway bridge at Remagen before German demolition charges could destroy it. It gave the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> their first crossing of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-9">9 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">US firebombing raid devastates Tokyo</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In the night of 9-10 March, some 300 B-29 bombers dropped incendiaries on Tokyo, burning about 41 square kilometres. Around 100,000 people died, the deadliest air raid in history.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-19">19 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Hitler issues the 'Nero Decree'</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Hitler ordered the destruction of German industry, transport and supplies before they fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a>. Armaments Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-speer">Albert Speer</a> worked to ensure it was largely not carried out.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-22">22 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Arab League founded in Cairo</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, Transjordan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a>, Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> signed the pact founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arab-league">League of Arab States</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> joining soon after. It now has 22 members.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-1">1 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">US forces land on Okinawa</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">American troops came ashore on Okinawa in Operation Iceberg, the largest amphibious assault of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-war">Pacific War</a>. The 82-day battle that followed cost the lives of well over 100,000 soldiers and civilians.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-war">Pacific War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-9">9 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Dietrich Bonhoeffer is executed at Flossenbürg</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Lutheran pastor and theologian Dietrich Bonhoeffer was hanged on Hitler's orders for his links to the resistance. He died a month before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s surrender.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-11">11 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">US troops reach Buchenwald concentration camp</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">American soldiers arrived at Buchenwald near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar">Weimar</a>, where prisoners had already taken control of the camp. Some 56,000 people had died there; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwight-d-eisenhower">Eisenhower</a> later had local Germans brought to see it.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-12">12 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Franklin D. Roosevelt dies at Warm Springs</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franklin-d-roosevelt">Franklin D. Roosevelt</a> died of a cerebral haemorrhage in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> early in his fourth term. Harry Truman became president and presided over the end of the war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and the Pacific.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-27">27 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Partisans capture Mussolini at Dongo</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Disguised in a German greatcoat in a convoy heading north, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Benito Mussolini</a> was recognised and seized by Italian partisans near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-como">Lake Como</a>. He was shot the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Benito Mussolini</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-28">28 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Partisans shoot Mussolini near Lake Como</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Benito Mussolini</a> and Clara Petacci were shot by partisans at Giulino di Mezzegra. The next day their bodies were hung upside down in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>'s Piazzale Loreto.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Benito Mussolini</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-29">29 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">US troops liberate Dachau</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">American soldiers entered Dachau, the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concentration-camp">concentration camp</a>, opened in 1933. They found more than 30,000 prisoners and thousands of bodies.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-30">30 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Adolf Hitler takes his own life in Berlin</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">With Soviet troops closing in, Hitler shot himself in his bunker beneath the Reich Chancellery. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> surrendered unconditionally a week later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-2">2 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Berlin garrison surrenders to the Red Army</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">General Helmuth Weidling surrendered the German forces in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> to the Soviets two days after Hitler's suicide. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s unconditional surrender followed within a week.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-7">7 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Germany signs its unconditional surrender at Reims</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">General Alfred Jodl signed the surrender at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwight-d-eisenhower">Eisenhower</a>'s headquarters, to take effect the next night. A second signing in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> followed at Soviet insistence.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/london" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/london.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-8">8 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Allies celebrate Victory in Europe Day</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s surrender took effect and crowds filled the streets of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, where the surrender came after midnight, victory is marked on 9 May.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-26">26 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">United Nations Charter is signed in San Francisco</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates of 50 nations signed the Charter creating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> to maintain peace and security. It came into force in October 1945.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-16">16 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The first atomic bomb is detonated in New Mexico</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Trinity test at 5.29 am in the Jornada del Muerto desert proved the plutonium bomb worked. Oppenheimer later recalled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhagavad-gita">Bhagavad Gita</a>: 'Now I am become Death, the destroyer of worlds.'</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-17">17 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Potsdam Conference opens</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Truman, Stalin and Churchill, later replaced by Attlee, met at Cecilienhof near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>. They settled the occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and issued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potsdam-declaration">Potsdam Declaration</a> demanding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s unconditional surrender.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hiroshima.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-6">6 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">US bomber drops the atomic bomb on Hiroshima</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The B-29 Enola Gay dropped a uranium bomb on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima">Hiroshima</a>, the first nuclear weapon used in war. Some 70,000 people died at once and perhaps 140,000 by the end of 1945.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima">Hiroshima</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/moscow" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moscow.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-8">8 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Soviet Union declares war on Japan</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> declared war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and, within hours, launched a massive invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a>. Coming between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atomic-bombings-of-hiroshima-and-nagasaki">atomic bombings</a>, it helped persuade Japan's leaders to surrender.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/nagasaki" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nagasaki.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-9">9 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">US bomber drops an atomic bomb on Nagasaki</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The plutonium bomb Fat Man exploded over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagasaki">Nagasaki</a>, killing some 40,000 people at once and many more later. Six days later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> announced its surrender.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagasaki">Nagasaki</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-10">10 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Japan offers to surrender if the Emperor is preserved</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After an imperial intervention, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> told the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> it would accept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potsdam">Potsdam</a> terms provided the Emperor's prerogatives were kept. The US reply left his status to the Allied commander and the Japanese people.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hirohito" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hirohito.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-14">14 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Japan accepts the Allied terms of surrender</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s government notified the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> that it accepted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potsdam-declaration">Potsdam Declaration</a>, and President Truman announced the news that evening. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hirohito">Emperor Hirohito</a> recorded a broadcast to his people for the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hirohito">Hirohito</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hirohito" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hirohito.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-15">15 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Hirohito broadcasts Japan's surrender</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">For the first time, ordinary Japanese heard their emperor's voice as he announced acceptance of the Allied terms. The day is marked as VJ Day in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>; the formal surrender was signed on 2 September.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hirohito">Hirohito</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/indonesian-independence" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/indonesian-independence.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-17">17 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Sukarno proclaims Indonesian independence</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Two days after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s surrender, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukarno">Sukarno</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammad-hatta">Mohammad Hatta</a> proclaimed independence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jakarta">Jakarta</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> fought to return, but transferred <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> in 1949.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesian-independence">Indonesian independence</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-world-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-2">2 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Japan signs the instrument of surrender aboard USS Missouri</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Japanese envoys signed the formal surrender in Tokyo Bay before General MacArthur and Allied representatives. The ceremony officially ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uss-missouri">USS Missouri</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-24">24 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The United Nations comes into being</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations-charter">United Nations Charter</a> entered into force once a majority of signatories, including the five permanent Security Council members, had ratified it. The date is celebrated annually as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> Day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/london" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/london.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-16">16 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">UNESCO's constitution is signed in London</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates of 37 countries signed the constitution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization</a>. It promotes cooperation in education, science and culture and lists World Heritage Sites.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nuremberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-20">20 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Nuremberg trials begin</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The International Military Tribunal opened at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a> to try 22 senior Nazi leaders for war crimes, crimes against peace and crimes against humanity. The trial laid foundations for international criminal law.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/august-revolution" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/august-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolution</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/august-revolution">August Revolution</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The August Revolution was the seizure of power across Vietnam by the Viet Minh in August 1945, after Japan's surrender at the end of the Second World War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/setif-and-guelma-massacre">Sétif and Guelma massacre</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Sétif and Guelma massacre followed demonstrations on 8 May 1945, VE Day, in the town of Sétif in French Algeria, where nationalist marchers clashed with police and rioting killed about a hundred Europeans.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/atomic-bombings-of-hiroshima-and-nagasaki" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/atomic-bombings-of-hiroshima-and-nagasaki.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/atomic-bombings-of-hiroshima-and-nagasaki">Atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki were the attacks by the United States on two Japanese cities in August 1945, the only uses of nuclear weapons in war.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-surabaya" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-surabaya.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-surabaya">Battle of Surabaya</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Surabaya was fought in October and November 1945 in the East Javanese port of Surabaya between Indonesian nationalist fighters and British and British Indian troops sent to accept the Japanese surrender.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/berlin-declaration-1945" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/berlin-declaration-1945.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/berlin-declaration-1945">Berlin Declaration (1945)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Berlin Declaration of 5 June 1945 was issued by the four Allied commanders, Eisenhower, Zhukov, Montgomery and de Lattre de Tassigny, after Germany's unconditional surrender.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/bleiburg-repatriations" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bleiburg-repatriations.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/bleiburg-repatriations">Bleiburg repatriations</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Bleiburg repatriations took place in May 1945, when British forces in southern Austria refused the surrender of retreating soldiers of the Independent State of Croatia and accompanying civilians near the town of Bleiburg and handed them over to Yugoslav…</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/potsdam-agreement" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/potsdam-agreement.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/potsdam-agreement">Potsdam Agreement</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Potsdam Agreement was signed on 1 August 1945 at the end of the Potsdam Conference between the United States, the Soviet Union and the United Kingdom.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/potsdam-declaration" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/potsdam-declaration.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/potsdam-declaration">Potsdam Declaration</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Potsdam Declaration was the statement issued on 26 July 1945 by the United States, Britain and China setting out the terms for Japan's surrender in the Second World War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-iwo-jima">Battle of Iwo Jima</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Iwo Jima was fought from 19 February to 26 March 1945, when United States Marines captured the volcanic island of Iwo Jima from Japan in the Pacific War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-okinawa" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-okinawa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-okinawa">Battle of Okinawa</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Okinawa was fought from April to June 1945 between American and Japanese forces on Okinawa, the largest battle of the Pacific War on Japanese territory.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/soviet-declaration-of-war-on-japan">Soviet declaration of war on Japan</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Soviet declaration of war on Japan was made in August 1945, followed by a rapid Soviet invasion of Japanese-held Manchuria.</p></div></li></ol></section>
